# The files of this repository that the ios-16.5 kernel tree takes at build time (xnu/fork.sh, the profile's fork_copy):
# "SOURCE TARGET", SOURCE from the repository root, TARGET in the tree.
#
# GenericARMPE.cpp: sleep_cores=1 on the S9. The fork's file asks the CPU topology for CLUSTER_TYPE_P, but the loader's
# device tree does not name a cluster type: every core is CLUSTER_TYPE_SMP, so sleep_cores=1 chose none and the M3s
# stayed online (the 13 November run: cpufreq_gov still said "big ... 4 online"). The copy also logs the display and
# park/unpark lines through hakios_say(), the loader's log: printf from this file does not reach the serial console.
xnu/files/GenericARMPE.cpp iokit/Kernel/GenericARMPE.cpp

# The ninth run (14 November): all four M3s answered CPU_ON with 0 and only cpu 3's "stage 1" ever appeared;
# unpark() still said "started again" after 5.1 s, the exit mask was cleared, and the governor's measuring
# thread bound to the dead core and stopped. The three copies below are the fork's files at the pinned commit
# with the start's failure made to reach processor_startup() (which returns the processor to PROCESSOR_OFF_LINE
# instead of leaving it in PROCESSOR_START) and the firmware's answers logged: AFFINITY_INFO before a restart,
# the last stage and AFFINITY_INFO after the 5 s wait, and a CPU_OFF that returns.
xnu/files/cpu.c osfmk/arm64/cpu.c
xnu/files/hakios_p125.h osfmk/kern/hakios_p125.h
xnu/files/hakios_p125_impl.h osfmk/arm64/hakios_p125_impl.h
xnu/files/processor.c osfmk/kern/processor.c
xnu/files/psci_smp.c osfmk/arm64/psci_smp.c
# Core PSCI cannot depend on BSD's sys/ include path. Install the exact
# shared ABI in osfmk as well as the BSD driver-map destination.
drivers/soc/exynos/hakios.p8_soc_snapshot.h osfmk/arm64/hakios.p8_soc_snapshot.h
